{title: Guarding My Path}
{subtitle: Psalms 119:9–11}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm] | [Ab] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]How can [Bb/D]a young man keep his [Cm]path pure
By [Ab]guarding it accord[Bb]ing to your [Eb]word
With all my [Bb/D]heart I seek [Cm]you now
Do not [Ab]let me stray from your command[Bb]ments
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I [Ab]have stored up [Bb]your word in [Eb]my heart
[Ab]So that I [Bb]may not sin against [Cm]you
[Ab]Your law is [Bb]the light of [Cm]my feet
[Bb6]Guiding me [Ab]through the [Bb]night
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]I will [Bb/D]thank you with an up[Cm]right heart
[Ab]As I learn [Bb]your righteous judg[Eb]ments
I will keep [Bb/D]your statutes [Cm]close
Do not [Ab]utterly forsake me [Bb]here
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Blessed are [Bb]you Lord teach me [Eb]your statutes
[Ab]With my lips [Bb]I recount all the [Cm]judgments
In the [Ab]way of your tes[Bb]timonies I re[Cm]joice
As [Ab]over all riches in the [Bb]world
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Guarding it [Bb/D]according to [Cm]your word
My [Ab]heart is [Bb]safe within your [Eb]law
{end_of_verse}
